meta {
  name: Get Files in Submission Attribute Metadata
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

get {
  url: {{CRM_URL}}/EntityDefinitions(LogicalName='rpa_onlinesubmission')/Attributes(LogicalName='rpa_filesinsubmission')?$select=LogicalName,SchemaName,AttributeType,AttributeTypeName,SourceType,IsValidForCreate,IsValidForUpdate
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  $select: LogicalName,SchemaName,AttributeType,AttributeTypeName,SourceType,IsValidForCreate,IsValidForUpdate
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: false
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Settles blocking decision B1 in
  plans/files-in-submission-crm-mapping-20260827-1612.md: the logical name
  and data type of the "Files in Submission" field shown as required but
  empty on the Online Submission form.

  h4. Answer

    LogicalName        rpa_filesinsubmission
    SchemaName         rpa_FilesinSubmission
    AttributeType      Integer (IntegerAttributeMetadata)
    SourceType         0, a plain attribute
    IsValidForCreate   true
    IsValidForUpdate   true

  Three consequences. Integer means fcp-sfd-crm must send a JSON number, not
  a string. Both existing writers in the estate
  (ffc-ice-crm/app/services/crm-client.js:42 and
  fcp-sfd-core/resources/crm/crm-dev.json:548) send a quoted string and rely
  on Dataverse coercing it, so neither is a safe template to copy.
  SourceType 0 means the attribute is plain rather than calculated or
  rollup, so Dynamics does not own the value and the service must write it.
  IsValidForCreate true means the create-only write with If-None-Match: '*'
  holds, so no PATCH path is needed.

  h4. Why the attribute is addressed by key

  The attribute is reached directly, as
  Attributes(LogicalName='rpa_filesinsubmission'), rather than by filtering
  the attribute collection. Metadata entities do not support the startswith
  function, so a name-prefix search fails outright with

    The "startswith" function isn't supported for Metadata Entities
    (code 0x8006088a)

  and DisplayName cannot be filtered server-side either, being a complex
  type. Addressing by key avoids the question. To search by label rather
  than by name, use "List All Attributes on rpa_onlinesubmission" and scan
  the result by eye.

  h4. MaxLength

  Deliberately absent from the $select. It is exposed only on
  StringAttributeMetadata, so selecting it on the base type fails the whole
  request, and on an Integer attribute it does not apply in any case. Use
  "Get String Attribute MaxLength" for string attributes.

  h4. Per environment

  Re-run this against each environment before promoting the write into it.
  The attribute is solution-deployed, so its presence in SANDBOX proves
  nothing about TEST, UAT or PRODUCTION.
}
